      "text": "Jamie's jar contains the same number of each coin: nickels, dimes, and quarters.\nLet's assume that Jamie has x nickels, x dimes, and x quarters.\nEach nickel is worth 5 cents, so the total value of the nickels is 5x * x = 5x^2.\nEach dime is worth 10 cents, so the total value of the dimes is 10x * x = 10x^2.\nEach quarter is worth 25 cents, so the total value of the quarters is 25x * x = 25x^2.\nIn total, Jamie's jar has x nickels + x dimes + x quarters = x(11x^2) = 11x^3.\nHence, 11x^3 = 1320.\nDivide both sides of the equation by 11: x^3 = 120/11.\nSince x has to be an integer, the only possible value for x is 5, because 120/11 > 11 for values between 12 and 11^2.\nTherefore, Jamie has 5 nickels in his jar.",
